  "title": "lwres: Do not claim (unregistered) port 921",
  "description": "Bind9 removed lwresd and liblwres in September of 2017, with the\nrelease of Bind 9.12.0 Alpha:\nhttps://www.isc.org/blogs/bind-9-12-0-alpha/\nhttps://gitlab.isc.org/isc-projects/bind9/-/commit/8eb88aafee951859264e36c315b1289cd8c2088b\n\nBy default, lwresd used UDP port 921, which was never IANA assigned,\nalthough that didn't matter much because lwresd only listened on the\nIPv4 loopback interface. As the dissector does not check the address\nnor do any other sort of heuristics, remove the default port assignment.\nSome long lived Linux distributions (e.g., Debian Bullseye) may still\nhave it installed, but it should not be that common.",
